# Instagram OAuth Test Endpoints
# These endpoints can be used to test the Instagram OAuth functionality

# 1. Initiate Instagram OAuth
# This endpoint redirects the user to Instagram for authentication
GET {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/auth/instagram

### Expected Response:
# 302 Redirect to Instagram OAuth URL with the following parameters:
# - client_id: INSTAGRAM_APP_ID from environment
# - redirect_uri: INSTAGRAM_CALLBACK_URL from environment  
# - scope: instagram_business_basic
# - response_type: code

---

# 2. Instagram OAuth Callback
# This endpoint handles the callback from Instagram after user authorization
# Note: This endpoint is typically called by Instagram, not directly
GET {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/auth/instagram/callback?code=AUTH_CODE_HERE

### Expected Response:
# 302 Redirect to frontend with token:
# REDIRECT_URL: {{FRONTEND_URL}}/auth/instagram/callback?token=JWT_TOKEN&success=true

### If there's an error:
# REDIRECT_URL: {{FRONTEND_URL}}/auth/instagram/callback?success=false&error=ERROR_MESSAGE

---

# Environment Configuration Required:
# INSTAGRAM_APP_ID=1199927542002046
# INSTAGRAM_APP_SECRET=b14e747f0b275047d35dc22665791528
# INSTAGRAM_CALLBACK_URL=https://health-platform-backend-production.up.railway.app/api/v1/auth/instagram/callback

### Instagram OAuth Flow:
# 1. User clicks "Login with Instagram" on frontend
# 2. Frontend calls GET /api/v1/auth/instagram
# 3. Server redirects to Instagram OAuth URL
# 4. User authorizes the app on Instagram
# 5. Instagram redirects to /api/v1/auth/instagram/callback with authorization code
# 6. Server exchanges code for access token
# 7. Server fetches Instagram user profile
# 8. Server finds or creates user in database
# 9. Server generates JWT token
# 10. Server redirects to frontend with token

### Testing Steps:
# 1. Ensure Instagram app is configured with the callback URL
# 2. Ensure environment variables are set
# 3. Start the backend server
# 4. Open browser and navigate to the initiate endpoint
# 5. Complete Instagram authorization
# 6. Check if redirected back to frontend with success token